# --stick-response console: the oracle reference's live stick response, a
# measurement, not a derivation; it is not a measurement of a DualShock.
# For every SDL axis value (-32768..32767) the byte the game read from the port 1
# analog pad when the reference test binary (third_party/duckstation-patches,
# applied head 3b91a21ba3e2559d67f743cd062f4d38e515de63) delivered the value through its live
# input path (regtest -bk2-phys) at its default settings, on every stick axis.
# Taken by tools/stick_response_measure.py: four sweeps (ascending, axes paired
# with the mirrored value, descending, each value followed by the centre), 65536
# values on each of four axes per sweep, every axis and sweep the same table.
# Regenerate (repo root, about 15 minutes): tools/stick_response_measure.py WORKDIR
# Power-on: an axis reads 128 for every value inside -96..96 until it first receives a value outside that range, and the table's byte from that row on in both directions; each axis latches on its own (checked at 0, +-50, +-96, +-97 and +-200 on three axes while the fourth stays at 0).
# Rows: first last byte - every value from first to last reads byte.
